## DO / DON'T
- DO use the exact size numbers above; the zone builders rely on them.
- DO give it the 3-4 recognisable features a person would name (a stone lantern: base, post, light
  box with 4 windows, curved roof, finial) — plus 2-3 pieces of wear or incident that make it look
  used: a chipped corner, a leaning post, moss at the base, a rope, a hanging tool.
- DO make `opts.variant` (0..n) change the SILHOUETTE, not just the scale: at least 3 visibly
  different versions (a different crown shape, a different roof pitch, a broken vs whole rail).
  Zones rely on this for variety, so a plain `variant` that only scales is a wasted asset.
- DO give any repeated natural asset per-instance hue room: expose `opts.hue`/`opts.tint` (or
  accept `opts.seed` and vary the colour from it) so 20 copies are not one colour.
- DON'T model a flat plane with a colour where the thing has real thickness (a fence is stalks and
  rails, not a textured quad) — closeups are judged.
- DON'T leave floating pieces: every sub-shape overlaps a neighbour by ≥ 2 mm.
- DON'T write anything outside the listed file(s).
